Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 09:17:53 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 27/50] debug.nmxgpu_dump: on-demand xe state dump; build
 stamp; build fails when fork_xe.py does

- xnu/nmx_diag.cpp: a real xnu sysctl; writing 1 runs the hook xe registers at probe
- override/xe/nmx_xe_debug.c: GuC CT, every exec queue with its scheduler entity and the fence it waits on,
  the GuC queue print, per-engine pending hw fences, the memirq source page
- NullMoth GPU: driving ... (build <stamp>), the stamp written by vm/tools/cycle.sh
- build-guest.sh: a step that stops before compiling (fork_xe.py anchor mismatch) is a failure, not stale objects
- temporary per-event job prints removed

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DP5dwQG4pUvK6V9ftNsQRB
